# SwiftFormat configuration — https://github.com/nicklockwood/SwiftFormat
#
# Verified against SwiftFormat 0.64.6 (the version CI and AGENTS.md §6 assume).
# Keep this file minimal and every option justified: formatting must be
# reproducible, so we pin the options that actually shape this codebase and
# leave everything else on upstream defaults.
#
# Language: Swift 6 language mode, strict concurrency (AGENTS.md §7).
#
# swiftversion 6.0
--swift-version 6.0
--language-mode 6

# Line width used by the wrapping rules. 120 is the limit SwiftLint enforces too.
--max-width 120

# 4-space indentation, no tabs.
--indent 4
--tab-width 4

# Trailing commas only in collection literals (valid in every Swift version),
# never in argument lists: keeps the sources buildable by older toolchains.
--trailing-commas collections-only

# `self.` only where the compiler requires it; SwiftUI view bodies stay readable.
--self remove

# Do not rewrite heavily indented switch cases; Xcode-style indentation only.
--indent-case false

# Build products must never be formatted or linted.
--exclude .build,DerivedData,.swiftpm,AniTV.xcodeproj
